# Admity environment configuration (EXAMPLE).
#
# Copy this file to `env.json` and fill in your real values, then run the app
# with:  flutter run --dart-define-from-file=env.json
#
# Do NOT commit env.json — it is gitignored. The Supabase anon key is a public
# client key (protected by Row-Level Security), but keep the file out of git
# anyway so project URLs / keys are not leaked.
#
# When you create a Supabase project, find these under:
#   Project Settings -> API -> Project URL  and  Project API keys -> anon public.

# --- The actual file you create (env.json) must be JSON, e.g.: -------------
# {
#   "SUPABASE_URL": "https://YOUR-PROJECT-ref.supabase.co",
#   "SUPABASE_ANON_KEY": "eyJhbGciOi...your-anon-key..."
# }
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The app runs fine WITHOUT these (offline-light mode): Supabase init is
# skipped and a warning is logged. Auth/data features simply stay inactive
# until you provide them.
